Gestione GPS
 Location Interval:
 Recommended: 3000 milliseconds (3 seconds) to 5000 milliseconds (5 seconds).
 Reasoning: Walking is typically a slower activity. A 3-5 second interval provides a good balance between accuracy and battery consumption. You don't need updates every second because the user's position won't change dramatically in that time.
 Min Distance:
 Recommended: 2 meters to 5 meters.
 Reasoning: A 2-5 meter minimum distance helps to filter out minor GPS inaccuracies and prevents the track from being too "jagged." It still captures changes in direction and movement. 2. Cycling
 Location Interval:
 Recommended: 1000 milliseconds (1 second) to 3000 milliseconds (3 seconds).
 Reasoning: Cycling is a faster activity. A 1-3 second interval is better to capture changes in direction and speed.
 Min Distance:
 Recommended: 5 meters to 10 meters.
 Reasoning: A slightly larger minimum distance (5-10 meters) is appropriate for cycling because the user is moving faster. It helps to smooth out the track and reduce the impact of minor GPS inaccuracies. Important Considerations
 LocationRequest.Builder(Priority.PRIORITY_HIGH_ACCURACY, 3000): Create a LocationRequest with high accuracy and an interval of 3000 milliseconds (3 seconds).
 setMinUpdateDistanceMeters(5f): Set the minimum distance to 5 meters.
 fusedLocationClient.requestLocationUpdates(...): Request location updates.
 fusedLocationClient.removeLocationUpdates(locationCallback): Remove location updates. In Summary
 Walking: 3-5 second interval, 2-5 meter minimum distance.
 Cycling: 1-3 second interval, 5-10 meter minimum distance.
 Battery Consumption: The location interval is the biggest factor.
 GPS Accuracy: Not perfect; use min distance to filter noise.
 Data Usage: More updates = more data.
 Fused Location Provider: Use it.
 Activity Recognition: Use it.
